WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:06.230
By coming this far, you have proven 
yourselves among the elite.

00:06.590 --> 00:09.680
The Academy Knights welcome you.

00:10.330 --> 00:13.820
I am Lorek Kugret, captain of the Knights.

00:13.820 --> 00:17.040
My sister, Loretta, 
is a first-year like yourselves.

00:17.040 --> 00:19.240
I hope you'll treat us both 
with the same regard.

00:19.240 --> 00:22.680
Oh, yeah! She's Miss Claire's 
Flunky No. 1, right?

00:22.680 --> 00:23.960
Don't call her that!

00:24.380 --> 00:27.840
And I humbly serve as vice-captain.

00:27.840 --> 00:29.460
I'm Lambert Aurousseau.

00:29.460 --> 00:32.470
Lambert is Lene's older brother.

00:32.470 --> 00:35.090
We'll be jumping right into 
our first order of business:

00:35.090 --> 00:37.470
the Foundation Day Fair.

00:38.970 --> 00:40.640
The Foundation Day Fair, huh?

00:40.640 --> 00:43.230
So I guess we'll be doing
something for the fair?

00:43.230 --> 00:46.730
Yes, the knights run a café there every year.

00:46.730 --> 00:48.800
It's a tradition at this point.

00:49.520 --> 00:54.780
A café? Does that mean 
I'll have to wait on people?

00:54.780 --> 00:57.310
But a regular café would be kinda boring.

00:57.310 --> 00:59.200
Let's mix it up a little.

00:59.200 --> 01:01.360
There's that bad habit of his again.

01:01.360 --> 01:03.290
Keeping it normal is perfectly fine.

01:03.290 --> 01:05.040
Rae, got any ideas?

01:05.040 --> 01:07.270
Well, let me think...

01:07.270 --> 01:10.920
The go-to themes would probably be 
a maid café or a butler café...

01:10.920 --> 01:13.730
<i>But neither of those would feel 
very novel in this world.</i>

01:13.730 --> 01:16.600
<i>And I have no interest in hot butlers.</i>

01:16.600 --> 01:19.800
If anything, I'd rather see 
Miss Claire in men's clothes...

01:19.800 --> 01:21.490
Hey, I like that!

01:21.490 --> 01:22.380
Huh?

01:22.380 --> 01:26.530
How about a café where the guys 
and girls swap clothing styles?

01:26.530 --> 01:27.640
What?!

01:28.110 --> 01:33.650
You mean the boys would dress as maids, 
and the girls would dress as butlers?

01:33.650 --> 01:34.890
Yeah.

01:34.890 --> 01:37.560
It'll still be a café, but with 
the guys' and girls' roles swapped.

01:37.560 --> 01:39.660
It'd be a fun twist on the norm, right?

01:39.660 --> 01:41.450
So you say,

01:41.450 --> 01:44.410
but is it acceptable for members 
of the royal family to do such a thing?

01:44.410 --> 01:46.500
Huh? Would it be a problem?

01:46.500 --> 01:48.460
It sounds like it'd be all kinds of problems!

01:48.460 --> 01:49.910
I think it'd be fine.

01:49.910 --> 01:52.670
Rod suggested it himself, after all. 
What could be unacceptable about it?

01:52.670 --> 01:53.920
Prince Yu?!

01:53.920 --> 01:57.880
I'd like to try dressing as a girl. 
It seems fun.

01:57.880 --> 02:00.140
Well, if that's how Prince Yu feels...

02:00.140 --> 02:01.180
Misha?!

02:01.180 --> 02:04.560
Miss Claire in men's clothes 
sounds so precious!

02:04.560 --> 02:06.310
Good job, Prince Rod!

02:06.310 --> 02:09.130
Yes, yes, of course you'd feel that way!

02:09.130 --> 02:10.350
But I'm against—

02:10.350 --> 02:15.500
Miss Claire, I bet Prince Thane will 
look beautiful in women's clothes.

02:15.500 --> 02:17.070
Wouldn't you love to see that?

02:20.940 --> 02:23.370
<i>Yep! She's so easy!</i>

02:23.370 --> 02:25.490
No objections from anyone else?

02:25.490 --> 02:27.690
No, I'm opposed to this idea!

02:27.690 --> 02:29.770
Just give it up, Captain.

02:30.370 --> 02:35.280
All right! So our festival production 
this year is a cross-dressing café!

02:35.280 --> 02:37.010
Yeah!

04:06.970 --> 04:11.980
<b>Episode 6</b>

04:06.970 --> 04:11.980
<b>The Secret Reason Must Not Be Told to Anyone</b>

04:13.710 --> 04:16.140
I let her talk me into this, but...

04:16.140 --> 04:18.300
I really have to wait on people?

04:18.300 --> 04:20.690
And in men's clothes, too, Miss Claire!

04:21.730 --> 04:24.610
Maybe it's not too late 
to voice my opposition...

04:24.610 --> 04:25.760
Miss Claire.

04:27.050 --> 04:29.830
You've been a very good friend to my sister.

04:29.830 --> 04:33.790
Lene has told me much about you, 
as well, Rae Taylor.

04:34.310 --> 04:37.860
I've also heard a lot about you, 
Master Lambert.

04:37.860 --> 04:40.420
Oh, you know about him?

04:40.420 --> 04:43.800
He's the magic tool specialist who takes 
care of all the academy's maintenance

04:43.800 --> 04:45.610
and inspections single-handedly.

04:45.610 --> 04:49.190
He's renowned as an inventor, too. 
Right, Master Lambert?

04:49.970 --> 04:52.560
I haven't done anything that special.

04:52.560 --> 04:55.330
Anyway, I wanted to ask a favor of you two.

04:56.560 --> 04:59.960
There have been more conflicts 
between students recently.

05:00.690 --> 05:05.700
Now that you mention it, some of the 
commoners have been doing peculiar things.

05:05.700 --> 05:09.360
Yes, and that has led to 
quite a few small fights.

05:09.360 --> 05:11.450
Goodness, how regrettable.

05:11.450 --> 05:15.170
The captain and I have had 
our hands full dealing with that,

05:15.170 --> 05:18.960
so it would be a big help if you 
could handle other matters for us.

05:18.960 --> 05:20.450
Yes, of course!

05:20.450 --> 05:24.160
I will take care of it all with great gusto!

05:25.830 --> 05:27.510
Thank you so much.

05:27.510 --> 05:30.950
So, what are these other matters?

05:30.950 --> 05:32.390
Well...

05:33.270 --> 05:35.640
It seems <i>something</i> has been seen here.

05:37.020 --> 05:43.010
Some have reported seeing a suspicious 
figure in the building at night.

05:43.430 --> 05:45.180
At the stairway landing,

05:45.860 --> 05:47.890
in the kitchen...

05:48.530 --> 05:52.410
And when the students 
on night patrol tried to approach...

05:57.290 --> 06:01.260
Later, they found a wet spot on their
shoulder in the shape of a hand...

06:03.230 --> 06:06.340
Oh? What's the matter, Miss Claire?

06:06.340 --> 06:08.100
Are you really scared of gho—

06:08.100 --> 06:11.970
D-D-D-Don't be ridiculous! 
I-I-I'm not scared at all!

06:11.970 --> 06:16.310
Um, if that's too difficult, 
I could give you another task.

06:16.310 --> 06:22.110
Hmm... We'll be using the kitchen to prepare 
test items for our café menu, though.

06:22.110 --> 06:25.180
Yes, but as of now, there are only sightings.

06:25.180 --> 06:26.730
No damage has been reported yet.

06:26.730 --> 06:28.110
I guess we'll leave it be, then.

06:28.110 --> 06:28.820
It...

06:29.160 --> 06:32.270
It's the Knights' job to protect 
the peace at the academy!

06:32.270 --> 06:35.100
We can't ignore any disturbance, 
however trivial!

06:35.100 --> 06:37.200
Oh? Miss Claire, do you mean...

06:37.200 --> 06:40.260
N-Nobles never go back on their word!

06:40.260 --> 06:43.720
Ghosts, spirits, whatever it is, 
I say bring it on!

06:44.590 --> 06:49.090
<i>Thus my occult night 
with Miss Claire began.</i>

07:02.210 --> 07:03.690
Well, this is it.

07:04.730 --> 07:07.360
I'll check the prep room in the back.

07:07.910 --> 07:10.250
Miss Claire, you check in here.

07:10.620 --> 07:12.740
Are you giving me orders?

07:12.740 --> 07:15.990
Would you rather go to the back, then?

07:18.890 --> 07:22.180
A-All right, fine! I'll give you this one!

07:22.180 --> 07:24.160
Great. I'm counting on you.

07:36.640 --> 07:40.310
Th-There's nothing here, right?

07:42.810 --> 07:45.820
Hmph! Of course there's 
no such thing as ghosts!

07:45.820 --> 07:48.580
They must have been half-asleep 
and seeing things that—

07:50.940 --> 07:52.850
Is something wrong, Miss Claire?

07:52.850 --> 07:55.490
S-Something got my hand all slimy!

07:55.490 --> 07:59.580
Hmm... It looks more gelatinous than water.

07:59.580 --> 08:02.430
It couldn't be the ghost 
he told us about, could it?!

08:02.430 --> 08:04.070
It looks like no harm was done.

08:04.070 --> 08:06.920
We'll send this for analysis, 
just to be sure.

08:06.920 --> 08:10.170
How can you be so calm right now?!

08:10.170 --> 08:11.840
Now, now, Miss Claire.

08:11.840 --> 08:14.950
You can just wash your hand 
and wait here for now.

08:17.370 --> 08:19.190
Academy Knights duty or not,

08:19.190 --> 08:22.220
I can't believe I have to spend 
a night in such a creepy place.

08:23.370 --> 08:27.120
<i>What if a ghost really does show up?</i>

08:27.120 --> 08:28.820
Miss Claire...

08:31.500 --> 08:33.450
Here you go!

08:34.050 --> 08:35.570
What is this?

08:35.570 --> 08:37.830
It's called fondant au chocolat.

08:37.830 --> 08:40.630
It's a kind of chocolate cake, your favorite.

08:40.630 --> 08:42.690
Why do you suddenly have cake?

08:42.690 --> 08:48.910
Also, chocolate is the latest confection 
just released by the high-end eatery Broumet!

08:48.910 --> 08:52.970
Now, don't worry about 
the little details. Just try it.

08:52.970 --> 08:58.450
Hmph! It would have to be on the same 
level as Broumet to impress me!

09:01.000 --> 09:03.030
<i>It... It's delicious!</i>

09:03.390 --> 09:06.240
<i>The cake is rich in chocolate flavor,</i>

09:06.240 --> 09:09.400
<i>and more chocolate oozes out from inside!</i>

09:09.400 --> 09:11.940
<i>It's irresistible!</i>

09:11.940 --> 09:15.150
Commoner! Which pâtisserie sells this cake?!

09:15.150 --> 09:16.460
This one!

09:16.460 --> 09:17.840
"This one"?

09:17.840 --> 09:20.630
Are you telling me... <i>you</i> made this?

09:20.630 --> 09:21.450
Uh-huh!

09:21.790 --> 09:25.540
I've been really into developing 
new recipes lately, too!

09:25.540 --> 09:29.940
When do you have time for that? 
You're at my service all the time.

09:31.370 --> 09:34.720
A suspicious figure that shows up 
night after night...

09:35.460 --> 09:38.120
Was the ghost in the kitchen actually...

09:39.510 --> 09:41.420
you all along?!

09:41.420 --> 09:43.390
Yep! You guessed it!

09:43.390 --> 09:44.720
Argh!

09:44.720 --> 09:47.140
You knew this all along, didn't you?!

09:47.140 --> 09:48.850
You betcha!

09:49.170 --> 09:52.860
Ta-da! I also prepared this for you!

09:52.860 --> 09:54.860
<i>When did she...</i>

09:54.860 --> 09:57.470
Wait! You only have one set!

09:57.470 --> 09:58.860
We can sleep together!

09:59.990 --> 10:02.430
This has taken a sudden turn 
for the ridiculous.

10:02.430 --> 10:04.740
I'm leaving once I finish this cake.

10:05.370 --> 10:08.080
Aw, you're not going to spend the night?

10:08.080 --> 10:09.580
Of course I'm not!

10:09.580 --> 10:11.960
We've solved the mystery 
of the ghost, anyway!

10:11.960 --> 10:13.460
Huh? But...

10:13.460 --> 10:18.480
I genuinely don't know what 
that mysterious hand was.

10:19.520 --> 10:23.310
S-Stop that! You won't fool me again!

10:23.310 --> 10:24.930
I'm not kidding.

10:24.930 --> 10:27.520
I'm going back right now!

10:28.060 --> 10:29.370
Miss Claire!

10:34.580 --> 10:37.570
It's here! I saw it!

10:38.570 --> 10:39.780
Ralaire?

10:40.650 --> 10:42.460
What? Ralaire?!

10:44.510 --> 10:47.100
You followed me here?

10:47.620 --> 10:51.120
Wait... So that damp handprint was...

10:51.120 --> 10:54.150
Oh, right! Ralaire's on a transforming kick!

10:58.030 --> 11:00.230
I'm leaving. This is stupid.

11:00.230 --> 11:02.640
Aw, Miss Claire!

11:16.780 --> 11:19.290
What? You're not leaving?

11:19.290 --> 11:23.280
I-It's not that. 
I'm just tired out from yelling.

11:23.630 --> 11:27.040
Well, come on! You're sleeping here, 
aren't you? So get in!

11:32.290 --> 11:35.250
Miss Claire, scoot a little closer.

11:35.250 --> 11:37.800
If you try anything funny, 
I'm kicking you out!

11:40.150 --> 11:43.080
Ralaire! Come over this way!

11:49.900 --> 11:51.910
Mother?

11:51.910 --> 11:53.220
Where are you?

11:53.770 --> 11:56.740
I don't want to sleep by myself.

11:56.740 --> 11:58.570
I'm scared.

11:58.970 --> 12:00.360
Mother!

12:04.360 --> 12:05.870
Miss Claire.

12:07.620 --> 12:09.190
Lene?

12:09.190 --> 12:12.450
Your mother won't be returning home tonight.

12:12.450 --> 12:15.180
The master is busy with work, as well.

12:15.610 --> 12:16.760
Oh...

12:18.890 --> 12:19.760
No!

12:19.760 --> 12:24.180
You and Father have to stay with me!

12:24.180 --> 12:28.680
I'm sorry, Claire, but we have to go.

12:28.680 --> 12:31.670
But today is my birthday!

12:31.670 --> 12:34.190
Is this more important than that?!

12:35.230 --> 12:36.480
Claire...

12:36.800 --> 12:39.920
Claire, don't give Melia a hard time.

12:39.920 --> 12:43.150
Nobles must always give 
priority to their duties.

12:47.890 --> 12:54.300
But I'm always so patient when 
you both have to go away...

12:55.120 --> 12:58.130
Can't you even stay with me on my birthday?

12:59.130 --> 13:01.710
I am truly sorry.

13:01.710 --> 13:04.380
I'll make this up to you, I promise.

13:04.380 --> 13:08.140
I know! I'll buy you a birthday present.

13:08.140 --> 13:11.810
You can have whatever you want. 
What should I get?

13:11.810 --> 13:14.100
I don't want a present!

13:14.100 --> 13:15.940
I hate you, Mother!

13:15.940 --> 13:17.000
Claire!

13:22.990 --> 13:23.920
Melia.

13:44.090 --> 13:48.090
Happy birthday, Miss Claire.

13:50.310 --> 13:54.240
Miss Claire, this is a present 
from all of us maids.

13:59.610 --> 14:01.250
Oh, it's beautiful.

14:01.250 --> 14:04.610
But I think it's a bit too big for me.

14:04.610 --> 14:08.550
It will be perfect once 
you've grown a bit more.

14:08.550 --> 14:12.870
Until then, why don't you use it 
to brush Lady Melia's hair?

14:15.810 --> 14:17.660
Yes, you're right.

14:17.660 --> 14:19.380
I'll do that!

14:21.810 --> 14:24.400
Now, shall we have dinner?

14:30.690 --> 14:32.940
Miss Claire! Miss Claire!

14:35.640 --> 14:38.650
Terrible news, Miss Claire! Miss Claire!

14:40.650 --> 14:44.350
The carriage was in an accident 
on the way back to the mansion...

14:44.350 --> 14:45.600
And Lady Melia...

15:02.670 --> 15:07.920
Miss Claire, you should eat 
something, or you'll get sick.

15:16.410 --> 15:20.640
Maybe if I die, I can be with Mother.

15:20.640 --> 15:22.530
You mustn't say that!

15:22.530 --> 15:25.150
Lady Melia would be so sad 
if she heard you say such things!

15:26.150 --> 15:31.260
I told Mother that I hated her.

15:33.910 --> 15:39.120
I had a fight with Mother...

15:39.610 --> 15:42.220
and that was the last time I saw her.

15:45.510 --> 15:48.920
I couldn't tell her I was sorry.

15:57.680 --> 15:59.310
Mother...

16:20.990 --> 16:22.080
Hey!

16:22.080 --> 16:23.580
Get away from me!

16:23.580 --> 16:25.040
Shameless girl!

16:28.790 --> 16:32.470
Oh, right. I talked with Master Lambert a bit.

16:32.470 --> 16:33.970
What? Really?

16:33.970 --> 16:38.930
Yeah. He seems kind, but he's 
also reliable, and very humble.

16:38.930 --> 16:40.730
Even though he's so talented...

16:40.730 --> 16:41.470
Exactly!

16:41.470 --> 16:46.140
My brother researches not just magic tools, 
but how monsters become familiars, too!

16:46.140 --> 16:48.730
He was made vice-captain 
because of his achievements!

16:50.480 --> 16:54.110
A-Anyway, I'm proud to 
call him my big brother!

16:54.110 --> 16:59.370
Really? Then would you mind helping us 
with our Foundation Day Fair prep?

16:59.790 --> 17:03.200
I think Master Lambert would 
appreciate it, too. Okay?

17:03.200 --> 17:04.330
Sure!

17:08.460 --> 17:10.390
This looks quite good.

17:10.390 --> 17:13.760
And this is the top pick for our menu 
at the Foundation Day Fair?

17:13.760 --> 17:15.840
Yep. Give it a taste.

17:15.840 --> 17:17.990
Let's eat.

17:21.870 --> 17:22.930
It's good.

17:22.930 --> 17:25.140
The flavor seems familiar somehow...

17:25.930 --> 17:29.080
I know! This is mayonnaise, isn't it?

17:29.080 --> 17:32.810
The new sauce that was 
just released by Broumet!

17:32.810 --> 17:34.610
You nailed it, Miss Claire!

17:34.970 --> 17:38.740
Broumet? How did you get that, Rae?

17:38.740 --> 17:39.900
Huh?

17:39.900 --> 17:44.250
Well, uh... I heard about it 
and tried making my own.

17:46.250 --> 17:48.250
Try these next!

17:48.250 --> 17:51.330
It feels quite lavish, with the meat 
as its central focus.

17:51.330 --> 17:55.170
You've done pretty good work for a commoner!

18:00.070 --> 18:01.480
Hey, Rae...

18:02.140 --> 18:07.040
Have all the recent new products from Broumet
been your recipes, by any chance?

18:08.140 --> 18:10.710
Oh, you mean the mayonnaise? 
I told you, I just—

18:10.710 --> 18:13.050
Even if you tried to make something similar,

18:13.050 --> 18:15.720
it wouldn't taste exactly the same.

18:15.720 --> 18:21.620
The quantities, combination, 
and steps would have to be identical.

18:22.880 --> 18:24.660
No, no, you're just imagining it.

18:24.660 --> 18:26.330
What about that meat, then?

18:26.670 --> 18:30.080
It was cooked rare, but most 
people would cook it through.

18:30.080 --> 18:31.980
That wasn't rare.

18:31.980 --> 18:35.880
It's called "rosé," and it happens 
when the hemoglobin in meat—

18:36.810 --> 18:41.740
<i>Well, crap. I had no idea Lene 
knew so much about the recipes.</i>

18:42.610 --> 18:47.520
Okay, I admit it. 
I've been giving Broumet recipes.

18:47.940 --> 18:51.520
<i>It's common sense to utilize one's skills 
from a previous life to turn a profit.</i>

18:51.520 --> 18:54.520
<i>Broumet is the only high-end 
eatery in this country,</i>

18:54.520 --> 18:56.030
<i>so the payoff was huge.</i>

18:56.470 --> 18:59.550
<i>Incidentally, chocolate was 
the first recipe I sold them.</i>

19:00.430 --> 19:01.410
But...

19:01.770 --> 19:04.090
I'd like you to keep this a secret.

19:04.090 --> 19:08.660
Why? Being the source 
of Broumet's recipes is amazing.

19:09.780 --> 19:11.970
I can't tell you all the details,

19:11.970 --> 19:13.720
but it's for Miss Claire.

19:14.420 --> 19:16.170
For Miss Claire?

19:16.170 --> 19:19.340
So please don't tell anyone, okay?

19:19.340 --> 19:23.550
Everyone has a secret or two 
that they want to keep, right?

19:26.900 --> 19:28.180
All right.

19:28.180 --> 19:31.550
But in return, teach me a recipe, too!

19:31.550 --> 19:32.690
A recipe?

19:32.690 --> 19:36.440
Yes! I want to make something for Miss Claire!

19:38.940 --> 19:41.400
Okay. Meet me here again tonight.

19:43.630 --> 19:44.570
Uh...

19:44.570 --> 19:47.330
Why is Miss Claire with you?

19:47.330 --> 19:50.320
Hmph. The two of you, sneaking around...

19:50.320 --> 19:52.500
You're going to make something again, right?

19:52.500 --> 19:55.960
So I'm taking it upon myself 
to taste it for you.

19:55.960 --> 19:58.670
I told you not to tell Miss Claire.

19:58.670 --> 20:01.490
I'm sorry. I just couldn't keep it from her.

20:01.490 --> 20:03.440
No helping it now, I guess.

20:03.800 --> 20:06.460
Miss Claire, it gets chilly at night,

20:06.460 --> 20:08.480
so let us know if you get cold.

20:11.250 --> 20:12.060
Hmph!

20:12.490 --> 20:14.190
Just make it already!

20:14.190 --> 20:15.560
Sure!

20:21.570 --> 20:24.570
The crème brûlée is all done!

20:33.290 --> 20:34.790
It's so good!

20:34.790 --> 20:36.790
This is really delicious, Rae!

20:38.800 --> 20:41.380
It's richer than regular custard.

20:41.380 --> 20:44.310
The crispy part on top is the best!

20:44.770 --> 20:46.960
I want some tea, Lene.

20:46.960 --> 20:48.090
Coming up.

20:54.890 --> 20:56.190
Lene...

20:56.670 --> 20:57.690
Here.

21:01.070 --> 21:04.230
Rae, this is the recipe for mayonna—

21:02.860 --> 21:04.230
Shh.

21:04.230 --> 21:06.700
Memorize it and get rid of the note.

21:07.120 --> 21:08.450
It's insurance.

21:08.450 --> 21:13.580
If... If you ever really 
need it, use that recipe.

21:21.750 --> 21:23.670
I want another one.

21:23.670 --> 21:27.170
What? Miss Claire, I think 
that would be too much...

21:27.170 --> 21:28.110
Now, now.

21:28.110 --> 21:31.330
Why don't you try making one more 
and call it practice, Lene?

21:38.260 --> 21:39.620
Are you okay?

21:39.620 --> 21:41.480
Yeah, it's not that bad.

21:49.390 --> 21:51.320
Thanks, Rae!

21:51.320 --> 21:52.990
You two are awfully close.

21:52.990 --> 21:54.950
You're jealous, Miss Claire?!

21:54.950 --> 21:56.950
Aw, I don't know what to say!

21:56.950 --> 21:59.920
N-No, I'm not! Don't get ahead of yourself!

21:59.920 --> 22:01.000
Oh, dear...

22:01.520 --> 22:06.270
<i>Even when nothing happens, 
these days are so blessed.</i>

22:06.270 --> 22:07.470
<i>And I...</i>

22:09.350 --> 22:14.720
<i>wished that they could last forever.</i>

23:46.770 --> 23:49.500
Here, Miss Claire! Read this!

23:49.500 --> 23:52.280
"Be delicious. Be delicious."

23:52.280 --> 23:55.010
"Love-love, squee-squee, I love you..."

23:55.010 --> 23:57.660
Wait, what in the world is this?!

23:57.660 --> 24:00.700
The Foundation Day Fair, i.e. our school fair!

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>Episode 7</b>

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>What Makes or Breaks a School Fair
Is the Cross-Dressing Café</b>
